{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-retrofit-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.79: `rates-retrofit`, the Rates-scale run of the On-Road Retrofit port -- THC, CO, NMHC and the PM2.5 total with EC, NonECPM, sulfate and aerosol water at running and start exhaust, for the single-unit short-haul truck (52) and the combination long-haul truck (62), every fuel MOVES adds, in Washtenaw County, DEFAULT domain, August 2020, weekday, hour 7, at `<modelscale value=\"Rates\"/>`, from the default database plus a USER INPUT DATABASE holding thirteen On-Road Retrofit programs (`inputs/washtenaw-userdb-retrofit.esm`).\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. OnRoadRetrofitStrategy.buildSQL updates BaseRateOutput (emissionRate, meanBaseRate) beside MOVESWorkerOutput, and RatePostProcessorRatesFirst.sql writes the rate tables from BaseRateOutput, so the factor reaches RatePerDistance through `rtRate_total` and RatePerStart through `rto_ratePerActivity`; RatePerVehicle is MOVESOutput over the population, `out_emissionQuant` through `rtDay_quant`. Measured before porting against the un-retrofitted twin `rates-retrofit-base` (moves.rs, not wired here): 69,615 nonzero RatePerDistance cells, 1,071 RatePerStart and 1,071 RatePerVehicle cells are the twin's times the predicted factor within 9.9e-06, and no child pollutant moves.\n\nWHAT IT REPRODUCES (PLAN.md §7.3.80, finding F91 fixed): every table, key set exact, no `cell_exception` -- RatePerDistance 79,560 of 79,560 (worst cell 6.5e-06), RatePerStart 1,224 of 1,224 (4.8e-06), RatePerVehicle 1,224 of 1,224 (1.1e-05), StartsPerVehicle 160 of 160 (8.1e-06), RatePerHour and RatePerProfile empty in both. Every cohort here but CNG has two to four regulatory classes (41, 42, 46, 47 on 52; 46, 47, 49 on 62), and every Rates capture before it selected the single-class gasoline passenger car on the per-speed-bin path: its RatePerDistance on road types 2-5 was 1.9x to 112x high (52,864 cells) until each class's per-bin rate took its share of the cohort (`rt_regClassRateShare`, BaseRateCalculator's `smfrRatesFraction`). Its un-retrofitted twin is `rates-retrofit-base`.\n\nTHE BINDINGS. `n_ratesScale` = 1 and `n_outputRate`, the (pollutant-process, road type, cohort) pairs across five road types, checked by `rateSurvivorCount`.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "rates",
      "user-input-database",
      "control-strategy",
      "on-road-retrofit"
    ]
  },
